From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow low memory host datapath from DT

IPQ5332 AHB selects the default QMI firmware mode even on a 512 MiB
dual-radio board. Its host rings therefore use the large profile. Let
boards opt into the existing 512 MiB datapath parameters without changing
the fixed firmware memory contract, WMI peer/vdev capacity, or other boards.

qcom,ath12k-low-memory is a local boolean DT extension. Store a per-base
profile copy so the override is immutable after pre-init and shared static
profiles are never modified.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1839,6 +1839,17 @@ int ath12k_core_pre_init(struct ath12k_b
 	const struct ath12k_mem_profile_based_param *param;
 
 	param = &ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[ab->target_mem_mode];
+	/* An integrated radio can have a fixed default-mode firmware layout
+	 * while sharing a small host with a discrete radio. Only reduce host
+	 * rings and descriptor pools; leave QMI and WMI capacity unchanged.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(ab->dev->of_node,
+				  "qcom,ath12k-low-memory")) {
+		ab->host_profile_param = *param;
+		ab->host_profile_param.dp_params =
+			ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_LOW_512_M].dp_params;
+		param = &ab->host_profile_param;
+	}
 	ab->profile_param = param;
 	ath12k_fw_map(ab);
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -1170,6 +1170,7 @@ struct ath12k_base {
 	struct ath12k_reg_freq reg_freq_5ghz;
 	struct ath12k_reg_freq reg_freq_6ghz;
 	const struct ath12k_mem_profile_based_param *profile_param;
+	struct ath12k_mem_profile_based_param host_profile_param;
 	enum ath12k_qmi_mem_mode target_mem_mode;
 
 	/* FIXME: Define this field in a ag equivalent object available
